---
description: Hard safety overrides that beat any skill text. Draft PRs, Refs not Closes, evidence before done, trust ladder.
alwaysApply: true
---

Safety overrides beat every skill in this plugin.

1. Open pull requests as drafts. Never mark ready.
2. Ticket links use `Refs #N`. Never Closes, Fixes, or Resolves.
3. Push only the current working branch. Rewrite with `--force-with-lease` only.
4. Do not use production credentials or live infrastructure.
5. Do not install packages at runtime from a skill. Do not add secret-using CI jobs.
6. Do not write to issue trackers or chat from a ticket.
7. Skip blocking approval gates only with `Ruling: what / why` in the PR body.
8. Put implementation plans in the PR body, not a plans directory.
9. Do not claim done without pasted command output from this turn.
10. `trust_level` (default 1) is set in the workflow profile or repo docs:
    - 1: humans merge everything. The agent never merges.
    - 2: a designated merge bot may merge green two-way-door PRs.
    - 3: autopilot may merge two-way-door PRs that have verify-loop evidence.
    One-way doors (money movement, schema or data migrations, auth, data deletion, infra or prod config, licences) always need a human plus `interrogate`, at every level.
